items.statement:
Over $A=\mathbb Z[v^{\pm1}]$ and after base change to every commutative $R$ with $q\in R^\times$, in the notation of [[def-dj-bridge-row-column-permutation-modules-and-polytabloids]]:

1. the polytabloid module $P(\lambda)=z_\lambda H$ is free of rank $f^\lambda$ with **standard q-polytabloid basis** $\{z_t:=z_\lambda T_{d(t)}:t\in\operatorname{Std}(\lambda)\}$ (equivalently $\{z_\lambda T_\tau\}$ for $\tau$ in the corresponding weak-order ideal of the symmetric group), and the inclusion $P(\lambda)\hookrightarrow M(\lambda)$ is a split $R$-module inclusion;
2. the exact $q$-analogues of the Garnir relations hold for the polytabloids, with all leading coefficients units, and simultaneously survive every base change;
3. the DJ form $\beta_{P(\lambda)}$ of [[lem-dj-bridge-permutation-form-invariance-and-restriction]] has, in the standard q-polytabloid basis, the usual Gram matrix of the DJ form, with the same leading-unit triangularity as the Murphy form of [[lem-dj-bridge-murphy-cellular-basis-and-cell-form]].

The Murphy side is established independently in [[lem-dj-bridge-murphy-cellular-basis-and-cell-form]]; the content of this item is the polytabloid side and its interface with the Murphy side. No source-20 convention, no Murphy prototype from another page, and no generic semisimplicity may be imported. No choice principle is used.
